The original is already minimal, so any speedup here will be marginal at best. This version computes the size once and returns `fields.data() + index` directly. That avoids going through `operator[]`, which can carry an assertion check under some standard-library debug modes. Behavior is unchanged: the same bounds check, and the same pointer or null result for every index.

```cpp
FieldDefinition* MesgDefinition::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
{
    const std::size_t count = fields.size();
    if (static_cast<std::size_t>(index) < count)
        return fields.data() + index;

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```

